  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: kafka-clients 3.6.2.rhlw-00004",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.apache.kafka:kafka-clients 3.6.2.rhlw-00004 with backported fixes for CVE-2024-31141, CVE-2025-27817, CVE-2026-33558, and CVE-2026-35554.\n\nCVE-2024-31141: Apache Kafka Clients: Privilege escalation to filesystem read-access via automatic ConfigProvider\n\nCVE-2025-27817: Apache Kafka Client: Arbitrary file read and SSRF vulnerability\n\nCVE-2026-33558: Apache Kafka, Apache Kafka Clients: Information Exposure Through Network Client Log Output\n\nCVE-2026-35554: Apache Kafka Clients: Kafka Producer Message Corruption and Misrouting via Buffer Pool Race Condition\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.apache.kafka:kafka-clients 3.6.2 from Maven Central.",
